# Story: someone glues Arbor to a launcher and a status bar. Windows are named by app, never by number;
# the window a name means is the one used last; a name that means nothing says so and changes nothing;
# and the small queries answer without changing anything.
# Spec: F50. Window ids start at 101.
open Safari
open Mail
open Terminal
open Safari
focus 101
focus 104
dock Safari left
expect ok
expect docked 104
expect floating 101
dock Mail beside Safari bottom
expect ok
expect above 104 102
dock com.example.terminal right
expect docked 103
zoom Safari
expect fills 104
expect hidden 102
# Named, it stays framed however often it is said; a shortcut's bare `zoom` would return.
zoom Safari
expect fills 104
zoom focused
expect ok
expect fills 104
windows
expect ok
where
expect ok
views
expect ok
displays
expect ok
version
expect ok
help zoom
expect ok
expect fills 104
expect count docked 3
# No such window, no such command, and an app that is called like a direction.
zoom Notes
expect fail
zom Safari
expect fail
zoom left
expect fail
expect fills 104
# The pointer names a window too.
show-all
cursor 1300 400
float pointer
expect ok
expect floating 103
